<SolutionPage
  title="Weight Management"
  parent="Muscle"
  oneliner="Lasting body composition change requires the right inputs at the right time — not willpower."
  slug="weight"
>
  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Weight management in men over 35 is rarely a simple calorie equation. Hormonal shifts,
    chronic stress, sleep debt, gut dysbiosis, and metabolic adaptation all layer on top of
    each other. What worked at 25 often fails completely at 45 — not because of discipline,
    but because the underlying biology has changed.
  </p>
  <p>
    My4MLife addresses weight through the Muscle pillar because sustainable composition
    change requires building metabolically active tissue, not just reducing intake. We also
    partner with a licensed telemedicine practice for individuals who are clinically appropriate
    candidates for GLP-1 receptor agonist therapy.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Body Composition Baseline</h3>
      <p>DEXA or BIA scan establishes lean mass and visceral fat — the metrics that actually matter.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Protein-First Nutrition</h3>
      <p>Hitting 0.7–1g of protein per pound of body weight daily is the single highest-leverage dietary variable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Resistance Training Prescription</h3>
      <p>Progressive overload 3–4 days/week is non-negotiable for metabolic health after 40.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>GLP-1 Telemedicine Lane</h3>
      <p>For qualifying individuals, our telemedicine partner can evaluate GLP-1 candidacy as part of a comprehensive plan.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <fragment slot="product-cta">
    <h3>GLP-1 Consult</h3>
    <p>Licensed telemedicine evaluation for GLP-1 candidacy — part of a full 4M weight protocol.</p>
    <a href="/consult" class="btn-sol secondary">Request Consult</a>
  </fragment>
</SolutionPage>
